## Euler buckling
'<small>Source: Prof. D. Vandepitte, Berekening van Constructies, Deel I, Hoofdstuk 5, art. 5.2-5.4</small>
'<i>The critical force for the four classic end conditions, and the Euler hyperbola that crosses the yield strength at a certain slenderness.</i>
E = 210000 N/mm^2'<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
I_z = 2003 cm^4', HEB 200<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
A = 7810 mm^2'<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
L = 4 m'<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
f_y = 235 N/mm^2', S235<span class="kolom-3"></span>'
N_E(β) = π^2*E*I_z/(β*L)^2
N_cr,a = N_E(2) to kN', cantilever, β = 2'
N_cr,b = N_E(1) to kN', pinned at both ends, β = 1'
N_cr,c = N_E(0.7) to kN', fixed and pinned, β = 0.7'
N_cr,d = N_E(0.5) to kN', fixed at both ends, β = 0.5'
i_z = sqrt(I_z/A) to mm
λ_b = L/i_z', slenderness at β = 1'
λ_p = π*sqrt(E/f_y)', the hyperbola crosses the yield strength here'
σ_E(λ) = π^2*E/λ^2
#hide
PlotHeight = 220
#show
$Plot{σ_E(x)/MPa & f_y/MPa @ x = 60 : 200}
'<span style="color:#D97706; font-weight:700;">━━ σ<sub>E</sub></span> &nbsp; <span style="color:#2563EB; font-weight:700;">━━ f<sub>y</sub></span> &nbsp; in N/mm², against the slenderness λ.
